// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`create-plugin macro prompt matches the creator prompt snapshot 1`] = `
"Help me create a new plugin. Use the bundled plugin-creator skill as your guide for the bundle layout and install steps.

First interview me to ground the plugin in a real need: what capabilities should the plugin bundle (skills, prompt commands, MCP servers, or a mix), when should it be used, and what configuration does it require? Ask clarifying questions before writing anything; do not invent a purpose I did not ask for.

A plugin is a folder containing a nessy-extension.json manifest describing the bundle, plus the component files it ships (for example a skill's SKILL.md, prompt-command markdown, or MCP server config). Choose a short, lowercase, hyphenated name and scaffold the bundle into a folder under ~/.nessy-agent/ through your normal file-writing tool so it goes through the usual approval. Keep the bundle minimal — include only the components the plugin genuinely needs.

Once the bundle is scaffolded, install it locally through the existing plugin install flow (the same local-folder / repository install the "Add plugin" flow uses) rather than any new mechanism, and fix anything the install reports. Confirm clearly when the plugin is created and installed."
`;
